{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:MassTheory.FrobeniusSelfPairingChirality","@type":"LeanModule","name":"MassTheory.FrobeniusSelfPairingChirality","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.Ring.Defs","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic"],"declarations":2,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.chiralityFactor_one","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.chiralityFactor_one","kind":"theorem","line":36,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/frobenius-self-pairing-chirality.lean#L36-L45","doc":"The chirality factor of the identity braid is `1` whenever the\nself-pairing of `1` is non-degenerate (`star 1 = 1` and\n`τ (1 * 1) ≠ 0`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.chiralityFactor","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.chiralityFactor","kind":"def","line":29,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/frobenius-self-pairing-chirality.lean#L29-L34","doc":"The **Frobenius self-pairing chirality factor** of `β ∈ A` with\nrespect to a trace `τ : A → R` and an antipode `star : A → A`:\n`a_K(β) = τ(β · star β) / τ(1 · 1)`. ","formalizes":[{"@id":"block:def:frobenius-self-pairing-chirality","label":"def:frobenius-self-pairing-chirality","md":"quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/frobenius-self-pairing-chirality.md"}],"signatureChunk":0}]}